# Bria, Riptide Rogue: "Prowess. Other creatures you control have prowess. Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, target creature
# you control can't be blocked this turn." On turn 3 Bot1 casts a Mox Emerald (a noncreature spell) with Bria and a Memnite in
# play: Bria gets +1/+1 from her own prowess (4/4) and the Memnite from the one she gives it (2/2), and Bria's trigger makes the
# Memnite unblockable. Bot2's Ornithopter, which cast a Mox Ruby on turn 2 with Bria in play, got no prowess (still 0/2) and
# may block Bria (and dies to her 4 power) but not the Memnite, so only the Memnite's 2 damage connects.

